{title: Take Heart, It Is I}
{subtitle: Matthew 14:22–33; Mark 6:45–52; John 6:16–21}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He sent us out across the sea [F#]and climbed the hill to [C#]pray
The [D#m]night came down around us and [B]the land was far a[D#m]way
The wind was hard against us and [F#]the waves were breaking [C#]high
We [G#m]were straining at the oars be[B]neath a black and starless [D#m]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In the fourth watch of the night he [F#]came walking on the [C#]sea
It's a [D#m]ghost, we cried in terror, there [B]was nowhere we could [D#m]flee
But his voice came through the thunder like a light ac[F#]ross the deep
[C#]Take heart, it is I, [G#m]do not be af[D#m]raid
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take [C#]heart, it is [D#m]I
Do [C#]not be af[B]raid [C#]
When [D#m]the wind is high [C#]and the water is wide
Take [B]heart, it is [D#m]I
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Peter said, Lord, if it's you, then tell me, come to [F#]you [C#]
He [D#m]stepped out on the water [B]and he walked a step or [D#m]two
But he saw how strong the wind was and he started [F#]going down [C#]
Lord, save [G#m]me, cried the fisherman, I'm going to [D#m]drown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take [C#]heart, it is [D#m]I
Do [C#]not be af[B]raid [C#]
When the [D#m]wind is high and [C#]the water is wide
Take [B]heart, it is [D#m]I
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]At once he reached his [C#]hand out and caught [D#m]hold of him
Why did you [B]doubt, why did you [C#]doubt
They [D#m]climbed into the boat and the wind died [B]down
[C#]Truly you are the Son of [D#m]God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Take [C#]heart, it is [D#m]I
Do [C#]not be af[B]raid
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
